course: dictionary
lesson: 3437
title: Eyeshade and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An eyeshade is something you wear over your eyes. Its parts tell you a lot: eye and shade. A shade keeps light away from something, like the shade on a lamp. So an eyeshade keeps light away from your eyes.
explain: The dictionary gives two kinds. A visor has a stiff brim at the front and is worn without a top, to shade the eyes from the sun. A soft mask is worn over the eyes to block out light while you sleep.
explain: The sentences give clues about which kind is meant. «Goalball is played 3 against 3 by athletes with visual impairments; everyone wears eyeshades so it is fair.» Everyone wears them, so they are about the game, not the sun.
explain: Look for the words near the eyeshade. «Sleep with an eyeshade» points to the soft mask. «A green eyeshade» from old stories is worn by editors and accountants. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: An eyeshade is something you wear over your eyes to keep light away from them.
fact: «Eyeshade» means a visor with a stiff brim, or a soft mask worn over the eyes to block light while sleeping.
fact: Tennis players and golfers wear eyeshades in the sun.
fact: On planes, travellers use eyeshades to sleep.
fact: In goalball, everyone wears eyeshades so the game is fair, and the ball has bells inside so players can hear it.
exercise: «Goalball is played 3 against 3; everyone wears eyeshades so it is fair.» Why do the players wear eyeshades? | To keep the game fair | To keep their hands warm | *To keep the game fair for everyone | To keep the sun out of their hair
exercise: Tennis players wear eyeshades when the sun is strong. What is the eyeshade for? | Keeping the ears warm | Carrying the ball | *Shading the eyes from the sun | Holding the hair back
exercise: «Sam wore an eyeshade to sleep on the long plane trip.» What is an eyeshade here? | *A soft mask that blocks out light | A bag for carrying books | A hat with a big brim for rain | A pair of shoes
test: «On a long flight, Sam pulled a soft eyeshade over his face to block out the cabin lights.» What does the eyeshade do? | *It blocks the light so he can sleep | It makes a loud noise | It carries his drink | It keeps his hair tidy
test: In old stories, newspaper editors wear green eyeshades. What kind of thing is an eyeshade? | A small lamp for reading | A type of shoe worn in the rain | A pen for writing | *A visor or a soft mask worn over the eyes
exam: Everyone in goalball wears ___ so the game is fair. Which word fits best? | *eyeshades | spoons | kites | sandals
